The MIDI parser and Fine40 instrument grouping adapt code and vocabulary
from YourMT3, Copyright 2024-2026 The YourMT3 Authors, under Apache-2.0.
https://github.com/mimbres/YourMT3

The bundled Base SQ encoder and decoder use the scalar_model tensors extracted
from HeartMuLa/HeartCodec-oss-20260123. The source checkpoint's model card
declares Apache-2.0 at the version used for extraction:
https://huggingface.co/HeartMuLa/HeartCodec-oss-20260123/blob/f0fdddaf2bf36e35b75c5656c4da511c6b3a4c81/README.md

The codec implementation adapts HeartMuLa/heartlib under Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/HeartMuLa/heartlib/blob/main/LICENSE

Only the scalar encoder, decoder, and their configuration are redistributed;
the music language model and diffusion decoder are not included.

Modifications in this distribution remove training and evaluation paths,
retain the V8 inference model, and add a standalone CLI and checkpoint export.
See LICENSE for the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Browser MIDI preview

The web editor loads smplr 1.0.0 by danigb from jsDelivr, under the MIT license.
https://github.com/danigb/smplr
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/smplr@1.0.0/dist/index.mjs

FluidR3_GM is by Frank Wen, Copyright 2000-2002, 2008 Frank Wen and
Copyright 2008 Toby Smithe. The original SoundFont is MIT licensed.
https://metadata.ftp-master.debian.org/changelogs/main/f/fluid-soundfont/unstable_copyright

Melodic samples are rendered and hosted by Benjamin Gleitzman. The source
project distributes these FluidR3_GM renderings under Creative Commons
Attribution 3.0 United States (CC BY 3.0 US).
https://github.com/gleitz/midi-js-soundfonts
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/us/

The Standard drum kit is rendered from FluidR3_GM by Henrik Berglund.
Its origin and rendering process are documented in the linked discussion.
https://github.com/henrikvilhelmberglund/midi-js-compat-soundfonts
https://github.com/danigb/smplr/discussions/47

The editor fetches these samples unchanged from their hosts for browser
preview only. Singing Voice programs 100 and 101 preview with GM choir
programs 52 and 53, respectively (all program numbers are zero-based).
This mapping does not change exported MIDI or model generation.

